$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(2):AMD
$DATUM Pd-containing gel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the isolation
experiments. Into a degassed supension of the pre-swelled gel catalyst
PdGel (25:1) (50 mg) in the 80% aq EtOH (50 °C, 20 mL) under Ar
atmosphere for 1 h, the arylboronic acid (3 mmol), potassium carbonate (6
mmol) and iodo- or bromoarene (2 mmol) were added. The reaction mixture
was heated to 50 °C (or 80 °C in the case of bromoarenes) under Ar
atmosphere (GC/MS monitoring). The reaction was quenched with 5% aq HCl,
extracted with ether, the organic layer was dried by magnesium sulfate
overnight, then after filtration the solution was evaporated. The crude
product was recrystallized from 20-40% aq EtOH and dried. 1,1'-Biphenyl
(a). 2'-Methoxy-[1,1'-biphenyl]-4-carbaldehyde (g). Yield 0.403 g (1.90
mmol; 95%) of white crystalline substance. M.p. 49.7-50.3 °C (Ref.6 54-55
°C). Elemental analysis: For C14H12O2 (212.25) calculated (%): C 79.23; H
5.70; found: C 79.02; H 5.67. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 10.05 (s, 1H,
CHO), 7.92 (d, J = 8.4, 2H, H-3), 7.70 (d, J = 8.2, 2H, H-2), 7.40 -7.36
(m, 1H, H-4´), 7.35 (dd, J 1 = 7.5, J 2 = 1.7, 1H, H-6´), 7.07 (t, J =
7.5, 1H, H-5´), 7.02 (d, J = 8.3, 1H, H-3´), 3.84 (s, 3H, OCH3). 13C NMR
(101 MHz, CDCl3): 192.21, 156.61, 145.20, 135.01, 130.89, 130.33, 129.85,
129.58, 129.43, 121.15, 111.53, 55.72.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM GC yield, 95% isolated yield, palladium embedded in cross-linked
polyhydromethylsiloxane gel prepared and used as catalyst, Suzuki-Miyaura
cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Modular Approach to Heterogenous Catalysis. Manipulation of
Cross-Coupling Catalyst Activity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Stibingerova, Iva; Voltrova, Svatava; Kocova, Sarka; Lindale, Matthew;
Srogl, Jiri
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2016), 18(2), 312-315

